I’ve seen similar issues with large JSON files. The built-in `json` module is convenient, but it struggles with performance at scale. Don’t overlook parsing when optimizing pipelines or cloud workloads—it’s easy to ignore until latency or memory spikes become a problem.

Switching to a high-performance parser can reduce parsing time and CPU overhead dramatically. Good practice to test different parsers in your specific use case and always validate against serialization risks.

